<title>SLOVAKIA: Slovak 13-wk T-bill avg yield rises to 14.84 pct.</title>
<headline>Slovak 13-wk T-bill avg yield rises to 14.84 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BRATISLAVA 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Slovak finance ministry 13-week treasury bills rose in an auction on Wednesday to 14.84 percent from 13.963 percent at the last successful auction of similar T-bills on January 23, the National Bank of Slovakia (NBS) said.</p>
<p>Bids worth 448 million crowns were accepted out of the total amount of bids of 648 million. In the last auction of treasury bills with a maturity of 13 weeks on February 20 the ministry rejected all bids.</p>
<p>				   April 9	   January 23</p>
<p> Bids accepted (SKK million)    448		   800</p>
<p> Bids totall		    648		 1,903</p>
<p> Average yield (pct)	 14.84		13.964</p>
<p> Minimum yield		 13.45		13.000</p>
<p> Maximum yield		 15.80		14.000</p>
<p>-- Bratislava Newsroom, 421-7-521-8402</p>
</text>
